    "intro_html":  "Vindaloo came to Goa with Portuguese sailors as a dish of pork preserved in wine and garlic, and Indian cooks turned the wine into vinegar and the garlic into a proper spice paste. That vinegar is what makes vindaloo taste like nothing else on an Indian menu. It is sharp and hot and deep all at once, not just hot. Each bowl carries 566 calories and \u003cstrong\u003e52 grams of protein\u003c/strong\u003e for about \u003cstrong\u003e$4.61 a serving\u003c/strong\u003e (at everyday cost).",
